{"url": "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/education/academic-programs/vagelos-institutes-biomedical-research-education-phd-programs/becoming-student/about-vagelos-institutes-phd-programs", "final_url": "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/education/academic-programs/vagelos-institutes-biomedical-research-education-phd-programs/becoming-student/about-vagelos-institutes-phd-programs", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-23", "text": "About the Vagelos Institute's PhD Programs | Vagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons\nSkip to content\nVagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons\nAbout Us\nEducation\nResearch\nPatient Care\nDepartments & Centers\nSearch\nVagelos Institute\u2019s Biomedical Research Education PhD Programs\nAbout Us\nAbout Us\nMeet Our Team\nFunding and Support\nAffiliated Departments, Centers, and Institutes\nNews\nEvents\nContact Us\nPhD Programs\nPhD Programs\nBiomedical Informatics\nBiomedical Life Sciences\nNeurobiology and Behavior\nBecoming a Student\nBecoming a Student\nHow to Apply\nWelcome From the Associate Dean\nAbout the Vagelos PhD Program\nOur Research Community\nCareer Services\nFinancial Support and Benefits\nOutreach and Visits\nProspective Student Frequently Asked Questions\nApply Now!\nLearn more about how to apply to one of the PhD Pathway programs.\nFaculty Mentors\nCurrent Students\nCurrent Students\nCampus Resources\nCareer Development\nCoordinated Doctoral Programs in the Biomedical Sciences\nCurrent Student FAQ\nFinancial Support and Benefits\nGraduate Student Organization\nImportant Offices\nMed-into-Grad Program\nPolicies\nStudent Clubs\nStudent Fellowships & Awards\nStudent Wellness and Wellbeing\nYou are here\nHome >\nEducation >\nAcademic Programs >\nVagelos Institute's Biomedical Research Education PhD Programs >\nBecoming a Student >\nAbout the Vagelos PhD Program\nVagelos Institute's Biomedical Research Education PhD Programs\nAbout Us\nPhD Programs\nBecoming a Student\nHow to Apply\nWelcome From the Associate Dean\nAbout the Vagelos PhD Program\nOur Research Community\nCareer Services\nFinancial Support and Benefits\nOutreach and Visits\nProspective Student Frequently Asked Questions\nFaculty Mentors\nCurrent Students\nAbout the Vagelos Institute's PhD Programs\nThe Vagelos Institute's Biomedical Research Education (VIBRE) PhD Programs are transforming biomedical graduate education\u2014integrating deep disciplinary training with an expansive transdisciplinary experience. As part of Columbia\u2019s Graduate School of Arts and Sciences and housed within the Vagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons, VIBRE thrives in a world-class scientific ecosystem. With access to over 350 faculty mentors and cutting-edge research facilities, PhD students engage in an unparalleled environment for discovery, collaboration, and innovation\u2014right in the heart of New York City.\nMade possible by a transformative gift from Roy \u201954 and Diana Vagelos, VIBRE empowers students to shape the future of biomedical science. Through its innovative curriculum, VIBRE fosters early cross-disciplinary training, enabling students to explore their passions, bridge scientific fields, and drive groundbreaking discoveries. VIBRE goes beyond scientific training and mentorship, offering career development resources and hands-on training in translating discoveries into real-world solutions, preparing students for careers in academia, industry, policy, and beyond.\nOur Model for Graduate Training\nPersonalized and Flexible Curriculum: Students can explore multiple fields through rotations and coursework before committing to a program/disciplinary track, ensuring a well-informed and individualized path to specialization.\nTransdisciplinary Foundations: Core courses reveal unifying scientific principles across disciplines, preparing students to tackle complex problems from multiple perspectives. Professional competencies further equip students with skills essential for success both within and beyond the lab.\nMentorship & Networking: A multi-layered mentorship program connects students with faculty, peers, and external experts, providing sustained guidance and support throughout their PhD journey.\nTranslating Science to Impact: Dedicated initiatives help students apply their discoveries to pressing biomedical challenges, working alongside clinical mentors and industry leaders to move science from bench to bedside.\nCareer Development: Tailored programs and workshops expose students to diverse career paths, leveraging New York City and Columbia\u2019s vast professional and alumni networks to prepare students for leadership positions across academia, industry, policy, and beyond.\nBack to top\nColumbia University Irving Medical Center\nNewYork-Presbyterian\nColumbiaDoctors\nAbout Us\nEducation\nResearch\nPatient Care\nInside VP&S\nFind People\nEvents\nAlumni\nCareers\nGive Now\nColumbia University Irving Medical Center\nVagelos College of Physicians & Surgeons\n630 West 168th Street\nNew York, NY 10032\nUnited States\nFollow Us\n\u00a9 2026 Columbia University\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and Conditions\nHIPAA\nGeneral Information: 212-305-2862", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/education/academic-programs/vagelos-institutes-biomedical-research-education-phd-programs/becoming-student/about-vagelos-institutes-phd-programs#cb-content__main"], ["Vagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/"], ["About Us", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/about-us"], ["Education", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/education"], ["Research", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/research"], ["Patient Care", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/patient-care"], ["Departments & Centers", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/departments-and-centers"], ["Search", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/search"], ["Vagelos Institute\u2019s Biomedical Research Education PhD Programs", "https://www.vagelos.columbia.edu/education/academic-programs/v